      "status": "pass",
      "cases": 38,
      "failing": 0,
      "failingDraftOnly": 0,
      "basis": "§4.2.4: \"defaultValue may return a String encoding (using the GraphQL language) of the default value used by this input value in the condition a value is not provided at runtime. If this input value has no default value, returns null.\" By Appendix A, a lowercase \"may\" keeps its RFC 2119 meaning, so the encoding is optional; the intent is plainly that a default is encoded, which makes this a SHOULD. A string that isn't an encoding of the default, or one for an input value without a default, still fails defaultValue."
